// Trusted specification stub for the standard-library runtime package.
// Gobra's bundled stubs do not cover runtime, and parallel.go calls
// runtime.GOMAXPROCS, so the declaration must resolve from an include
// directory. Every member declared here is an axiom: it is assumed, not
// verified, and must be listed in the trusted assumption register in the
// README one directory up.
package runtime

// GOMAXPROCS never reports fewer than one processor: with n <= 0 it
// returns the current setting without changing it, and the setting is
// always at least 1. The postcondition is load-bearing for crash safety:
// normalizeWorkers relies on it to establish workers >= 1, which in turn
// discharges the division-by-zero check on the chunk-size computation in
// parallelBestMoves.
ensures res >= 1
func GOMAXPROCS(n int) (res int)
